<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
%# Shared chrome: theme.css, fonts and favicon come from static.mailmasker.org
%# via homelab-webtheme, so a restyle needs no rebuild of this package. Only
%# the app-specific rules below live here.
%= include 'homelab/head'
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <style>
    /* MOBILE FIRST. The previous pass was a desktop layout with a media query
       bolted on, which is how the page ended up scrolling sideways on a
       phone. These are the base rules; the only media query widens things.

       THE SIDEWAYS SCROLL: a flex item defaults to min-width:auto, so it
       refuses to shrink below its intrinsic content width. A <select> whose
       widest option is a Maildir++ folder name like
       ".Tax Audit.Tax Year 2020 (123)" is therefore wider than the phone, and
       it drags the whole page with it. min-width:0 plus max-width:100% is the
       fix; the option labels are shortened in the template as well, so the
       control is not merely clipped. */
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-3) var(--space-8); }

    /* The one question the page asks. */
    /* Two buttons now, so this wraps: on a 360px phone the field takes the
       first line and Search / AI Search share the second, rather than
       squeezing a search box down to a few visible characters. One line
       again from 560px, where all three fit. */
    .askrow { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); }
    .askrow input {
      flex: 1 1 100%; min-width: 0;
      background: var(--black-primary); color: var(--text-primary);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      /* 16px: anything smaller makes iOS Safari zoom the page on focus. */
      padding: 0 12px; font-size: 16px; min-height: 44px;
    }
    .askrow button { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 var(--space-4); }

    /* AI SEARCH. Steel is already this feature's colour -- the AI badge on
       an answer uses it -- so the button that asks and the block that
       answers read as one thing.

       Outlined, not filled. Plain Search stays the primary action: two
       solid buttons side by side say "pick one" without saying which, and
       the cheap, private, always-correct one should look like the default.
       It is also the one that costs nothing per press. */
    .btn-ai {
      background: transparent; color: var(--silver-bright);
      border: 1px solid var(--accent-steel); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); font-size: var(--app-sm);
      cursor: pointer; transition: background var(--transition-fast);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .btn-ai:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--accent-steel); }
    .btn-ai:focus-visible { outline: var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .btn-ai:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; }

    /* The same two buttons at the foot of the open filter panel. Setting a
       filter is the moment you want to search, and on a phone the panel is
       tall enough that the real buttons have scrolled off the top. */
    .panel-actions {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2);
      margin-top: var(--space-3);
    }
    .panel-actions button { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 var(--space-4); }

    .searchbar { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }

    /* Everything else is folded away until asked for. */
    details.filters { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
    details.filters > summary {
      cursor: pointer; list-style: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
      font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--silver-dim);
      padding: var(--space-2) 0; min-height: 36px;
    }
    details.filters > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    details.filters > summary::before { content: '▸'; font-size: 0.8em; }
    details.filters[open] > summary::before { content: '▾'; }

    /* THE FILTER PANEL.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------
       SPECIFICITY RULE, and the reason this block was rewritten. The old
       CSS styled control nameplates with `.field label`, which is MORE
       specific than `.chk` (one class + one element beats one class). Every
       file-type checkbox is a <label> inside a .field, so the nameplate rule
       won every property it set: each checkbox rendered as a tiny uppercase
       muted word with its box stacked ABOVE it -- pixel-identical to a
       disabled control, which is why the whole panel read as greyed out.

       Nothing here selects a bare element inside a container. Every rule
       targets its own class, so a control added later cannot inherit
       another's look by accident.

       THREE WEIGHTS, kept distinct, because they were all the same before:
         .fsec-h  structural -- a rule with a word on it
         .lab     a nameplate over an input: small, quiet, sentence case
         .box/.chip  something you ACT on: full size, primary colour
    */
    .panel {
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      background: var(--black-primary); padding: var(--space-4);
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6);
      margin-top: var(--space-2);
    }
    .fsec { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); min-width: 0; }
    .fsec-h {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-3); margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
      color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .fsec-h::after { content: ''; flex: 1 1 auto; height: 1px; background: var(--border); }

    .box {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; min-height: 36px;
      cursor: pointer; min-width: 0;
      font-size: var(--app-base); color: var(--text-primary);
    }
    .box input {
      width: 18px; height: 18px; flex: 0 0 auto; margin: 0;
      accent-color: var(--accent-steel); cursor: pointer;
    }
    .box input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .row-chk { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-6); }

    .lab { display: block; font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); }
    .field { min-width: 0; }
    .field input, .field select {
      width: 100%; max-width: 100%; min-width: 0;
      background: var(--black-secondary); color: var(--text-primary);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      padding: 0 10px; font-size: 16px; min-height: 40px; font-family: inherit;
    }
    .field input::placeholder { color: var(--text-muted); }
    .field input:focus-visible, .field select:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: -1px;
    }

    /* Chips. Fourteen 18px boxes is a lot of small targets, and a filled
       chip reads across the panel where a tick does not. The real <input>
       stays in the markup -- keyboard, screen reader, and it submits with
       the script off -- stretched invisibly over the chip. */
    .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); }
    .chip { position: relative; display: inline-flex; min-width: 0; }
    .chip input { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; opacity: 0; cursor: pointer; }
    .chip span {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; min-height: 36px; padding: 0 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      background: var(--black-secondary); font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--text-primary);
      white-space: nowrap; transition: background var(--transition-fast), border-color var(--transition-fast);
    }
    .chip input:hover + span { background: var(--surface-hover); border-color: var(--silver-dim); }
    .chip input:checked + span { background: var(--accent-steel); border-color: #7290a6; color: #f2f6f9; }
    .chip input:checked + span::before { content: '\2713'; font-size: 0.85em; }
    /* Half selected: the family is on, but you have unticked some of its
       exact types. A different fill and an en dash, because "some of
       Pictures" and "all of Pictures" are different searches. */
    .chip input:indeterminate + span {
      background: rgba(74, 93, 110, 0.42); border-color: #5e7a90; color: #e6edf2;
    }
    .chip input:indeterminate + span::before { content: '\2013'; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .chip input:focus-visible + span { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }

    .daterow { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); }
    .daterow .field { flex: 1 1 150px; }
    .daterow .sep { min-height: 40px; display: flex; align-items: center; font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--text-muted); }

    .note { margin: 0; font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5; }
    .note.warn { color: var(--warning); }

    details.specific > summary {
      cursor: pointer; list-style: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
      font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-secondary); min-height: 32px;
    }
    details.specific > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    details.specific > summary::before { content: '\25B8'; font-size: 0.8em; }
    details.specific[open] > summary::before { content: '\25BE'; }
    details.specific > summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }

    /* Columns rather than a grid: fourteen groups of wildly different
       heights in a 3-column grid strand the short ones in tall rows.
       break-inside keeps a group whole. */
    .leafwrap {
      column-count: 1; column-gap: var(--space-6);
      margin-top: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-3);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      background: var(--surface);
    }
    .leafgroup {
      break-inside: avoid; min-width: 0;
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }
    .leafgroup h5 {
      margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider); color: var(--text-muted);
    }
    .leaf {
      display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; min-height: 30px;
      font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer;
      line-height: 1.45; min-width: 0;
    }
    .leaf input {
      width: 16px; height: 16px; flex: 0 0 auto; margin: 4px 0 0;
      accent-color: var(--accent-steel); cursor: pointer;
    }
    .leaf input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .leaf .m { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .leaf .ext, .leaf .qual {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-muted);
    }
    .leaf .n {
      flex: 0 0 auto; margin-left: auto; padding-left: 8px;
      color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--app-xs);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .leadnote, .leafempty { margin-top: var(--space-2); }

    .fsec-foot {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-3);
      padding-top: var(--space-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .aioff { opacity: 0.5; }
    .aioff input { cursor: not-allowed; }
    .clear {
      font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--silver-dim);
      min-height: 36px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .clear:hover { color: var(--silver-bright); }
    .clear:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .hint { font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); }

    .counts { font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------- AI mode */
    /* The consent dialog. Deliberately plain: this is a statement about
       where someone's mail goes, and dressing it up would be the wrong
       register. No scary colour either -- it is information, not an error. */
    dialog.consent {
      max-width: 34rem; width: calc(100% - var(--space-6));
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      background: var(--surface); color: var(--text-primary);
      padding: var(--space-6); box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
    }
    dialog.consent::backdrop { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); }
    dialog.consent h2 {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); font-size: var(--app-md);
      font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); color: var(--silver-bright);
      line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    }
    dialog.consent .cbody p {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--app-sm);
      color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    }
    dialog.consent .cacts {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2);
      justify-content: flex-end; margin-top: var(--space-4);
    }
    dialog.consent .cacts .btn { min-height: 40px; padding: 0 var(--space-4); }

    /* The answer. A panel, not a page takeover: keyword results stay below
       it and are what you fall back to when any of this fails. */
    .aibox {
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-steel);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--surface);
      padding: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }
    .aihead { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-3); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
    .aitag {
      font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
      letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider); text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--silver-bright); background: var(--accent-steel);
      padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    }
    .aians { margin: 0; font-size: var(--app-base); color: var(--text-primary); line-height: var(--leading-normal); }
    .aians.dim { color: var(--text-muted); }
    .airesults { margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; padding-left: 1.2em; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
    .airesults li { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--app-sm); }
    .airesults a { color: var(--silver-bright); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .airesults .meta { font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); margin-left: var(--space-2); }
    /* Model-authored TEXT, escaped like any other string and never markup. */
    .airesults .why { display: block; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--app-xs); }

    /* The standing indicator. It is here on every answer, not only at
       opt-in, because people forget what they switched on months ago. */
    .ainote {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2);
      margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; padding-top: var(--space-3);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted);
    }
    .aioffbtn {
      background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; cursor: pointer;
      color: var(--silver-dim); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
      min-height: 32px;
    }
    .aioffbtn:hover { color: var(--silver-bright); }
    .aioffbtn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }


    h2.sec {
      font-size: var(--app-xs); font-weight: var(--weight-normal);
      letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide); text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-muted); margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
    }
    .res { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .hit { padding: var(--space-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); min-width: 0; }
    /* Stacked by default: a subject and a date side by side do not fit a
       phone, and forcing them to produces the clipping this page had. */
    .hit .t { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
    .hit .subj { font-size: var(--app-base); color: var(--text-primary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .hit .meta { font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); }
    /* The file name is a link but should not look pasted in -- it is the
       heading of its own result, so it keeps the subject's colour and earns
       an underline on hover rather than wearing one all the time. */
    .hit .subj a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .hit .subj a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .hit .subj a:focus-visible { outline: var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }

    /* Download, immediately left of the name. Deliberately quieter and
       smaller: the name is the thing you came for. The padding is a tap
       target -- two links share this line, and on a phone a mis-tap here
       means a download you did not ask for. */
    .hit .subj a.dl {
      font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--silver-dim);
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
      padding: 4px 8px; margin: 0 6px 0 -8px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .hit .subj a.dl:hover { color: var(--text-primary); background: var(--surface-hover); text-decoration: none; }

    .hit .who  { font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--silver-dim); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    /* People and tags under a photo. The label carries the weight so the
       names read as content rather than as another grey metadata row. */
    .hit .who strong { color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 600; }
    /* The label once, then one branch per line beside it -- a two-column
       grid rather than inline flow, so a second branch starts under the
       first instead of running on behind a separator. With one branch,
       which is 88% of them, it is still a single line. */
    .hit .who.tags {
      color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--app-xs);
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2px var(--space-2); align-items: baseline;
    }
    .hit .who.tags strong  { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
    .hit .who.tags .tagpath { grid-column: 2; }
    .hit .who em { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: normal; }
    .hit .snip {
      font-size: var(--app-sm); color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 4px; overflow: hidden;
      display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    }
    /* Per-type metadata under a file hit. A definition list because that
       is what it is: a label and its value, repeated. Inline-wrapping
       rather than a table, so three fields on a phone are three chips and
       not a horizontal scroll. */
    .meta-kv {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px var(--space-3);
      margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: var(--app-xs);
    }
    .meta-kv dt {
      color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
      font-size: 0.6875rem; align-self: center;
    }
    .meta-kv dd {
      color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 var(--space-2) 0 0;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-width: 0;
    }
    /* The coordinate pair is the one metadata value that goes somewhere, so
       it has to look like it does -- a chip that reads exactly like its
       neighbours is not discoverable as a link. */
    .meta-kv dd a { color: var(--silver-bright); text-decoration: underline;
                    text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .meta-kv dd a:hover { color: var(--text-primary); }

    .acts { margin-top: 8px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-4); font-size: var(--app-xs); }
    .acts a { color: var(--silver-dim); min-height: 32px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
    .empty { color: var(--text-muted); padding: var(--space-6) 0; }

    details.pv > summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--silver-dim); font-size: var(--app-xs); min-height: 32px; }
    details.pv iframe {
      width: 100%; max-width: 100%; height: 320px; border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm); margin-top: var(--space-2); background: var(--black-primary);
    }

    @media (min-width: 560px) {
      .fields { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .leafwrap { column-count: 2; }
      /* Field and both buttons on one line, and the buttons back to their
         own width rather than splitting the row between them. */
      .askrow input  { flex: 1 1 auto; }
      .askrow button { flex: 0 0 auto; }
      .panel-actions button { flex: 0 0 auto; }
    }

    /* Wider screens only: the exact-type list in three columns, the result
       date back on the same line as its subject, a taller preview. */
    @media (min-width: 721px) {
      .wrap { padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-4) var(--space-12); }
      /* The search block is centred and capped; the RESULTS below stay full
         width, because a result list wants the room and a text field does
         not. Stretching the input to 1100px just made the caret start a long
         way from the text.
         560px holds roughly 70 characters, which is more than any query
         typed here. A literal 20% of this column would be 220px -- too
         narrow to see a phrase query while typing it -- so the intent is
         kept and the number is the readable one. */
      .searchbar { max-width: 760px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
      .askrow    { max-width: 560px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
      .counts    { max-width: 760px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; text-align: center; }
      .fields { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .leafwrap { column-count: 3; }
      .hit .t { flex-direction: row; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-3); }
      .hit .meta { white-space: nowrap; }
      details.pv iframe { height: 420px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
%= include 'homelab/header'
<div class="wrap"><%= content %></div>
%= include 'homelab/footer'
</body>
</html>
